            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 88-year-old female patient, admitted on 08/06/2024 due to acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. Treatment consisted of inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient was discharged in a stable condition on 09/06/2024. I recommend continuation of her inhaled maintenance therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Patient education regarding exacerbation management and smoking avoidance was provided. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
